This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is shard 'b' of layer-contract-conformance and inherits that fixture's reason without
qualification: the subject is scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh, which is not shipped to
consumers. On a consumer both directories printed a SKIP and exited 0, so the consumer's pool
recorded two `ok` verdicts on every push while nothing was tested.

A SHARD INHERITS ITS SIBLING'S MARKER BY CARRYING ITS OWN, NOT BY POINTING AT IT. The exemption
is derived per directory, so a shard without one is shippable by every reader that matters.
